  <ym-title|Local paid budgets and threshold
  selection><label|local-paid-budgets-and-threshold-selection>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, selected-scale trace producer.

    <item>Status: draft; two elementary selection arguments are proved. The
    primary, regular, and forced local atom estimates remain explicit
    analytic inputs.

    <item>Imported Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-local-paid-budgets.tex>.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Source crosswalk><label|source-crosswalk>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  content>>|<cell|<strong|Exact declaration and path>>|<cell|<strong|Checked
  correspondence and remaining status>>>|<row|<cell|Positive local budget
  choice>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.foton>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Cache.lean>>|<cell|The finite probe
  family is <verbatim|Local.tests>; the costs are the probe variation
  coefficient, regular-cost, large-support-cost, and primary-cost
  inequalities. The displayed choice (v=y/(2B)), (u=(1+sum q_\\tau)v) proves
  all four at once.>>|<row|<cell|Uniform stage
  thresholds>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.parliament>,
  <verbatim|YM.Push.PriceCompiler.eventually_transitions>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.decorate>,
  <verbatim|YM.Push.PriceCompiler.collect_upper>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Soot.lean>, <verbatim|Guild.lean>,
  and <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/PRICE_COMPILER/Basic.lean>>|<cell|At fixed stage
  (j), only <verbatim|StepStages j i> indices occur (the same stage and its
  predecessor); the coefficient degrees lie in <verbatim|Finset.range j>.
  Thus the eventual Medal conclusions intersect over finite sets.
  <verbatim|eventually_transitions> reduces the stage-index quantifier to
  those two cases, and <verbatim|collect_upper> replaces all stagewise
  thresholds by a monotone prefix maximum dominating the previous
  threshold.>>|<row|<cell|Bunk inequalities used by the atom
  estimates>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.Bunk>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Cache.lean>>|<cell|The four
  inequalities in the manuscript are exactly the fields <verbatim|cycle>,
  <verbatim|reg>, <verbatim|huge>, and <verbatim|main>, with (q_\\tau) the
  displayed <verbatim|chief> value. <verbatim|foton> chooses the two strictly
  positive budgets.>>|<row|<cell|Medal inputs and actual Stepper
  route>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.Cashbox>,
  <verbatim|.mosaic>, <verbatim|.primaryT>, <verbatim|.salaryT>,
  <verbatim|.gasT>; <verbatim|Soot.lean>, <verbatim|Kiosk.lean>,
  <verbatim|Harvest.lean>, <verbatim|Soil.lean>,
  <verbatim|Gas.lean>>|<cell|The selected local <verbatim|Stepper> is
  assembled by <verbatim|Cashbox> from the same-transition <verbatim|mosaic>.
  Its basis, regular, and forced fields are established by
  <verbatim|primaryT>, <verbatim|salaryT>, and <verbatim|gasT>.
  <verbatim|mosaic> requires the <verbatim|Bunk> and <verbatim|Medal> data,
  scale geometry, and history hypotheses. This unit proves the budget/tail
  threshold selection only; it does not reproduce those three local-card
  proofs.>>|<row|<cell|Medal construction
  estimates>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.decorate>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Guild.lean>>|<cell|The eventual
  Medal is obtained by intersecting the component estimates <verbatim|bairn>,
  <verbatim|decade>, <verbatim|fare_pr>, <verbatim|force_pr>, and
  <verbatim|sprited>; their quantitative hypotheses are listed in the
  declaration. The finite intersection is source-checked, while those
  component estimates remain assigned upstream proof obligations.>>>>>

  <section|Checks and open obligations><label|checks-and-open-obligations>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Read-only inspection: <verbatim|sed -n> on <verbatim|Cache.lean>,
    <verbatim|Guild.lean>, <verbatim|Soot.lean>, <verbatim|Kiosk.lean>,
    <verbatim|Harvest.lean>, <verbatim|Soil.lean>, <verbatim|Gas.lean>, and
    <verbatim|Push/PRICE_COMPILER/Basic.lean>; <verbatim|rg -n> locating the
    exact declarations and callers.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> cannot run
    successfully in this isolated clone because
    <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json> is absent; parent
    integration owns shared unit metadata.

    <item>No Lean source was edited; no Lean or TeX build was run.

    <item>Remaining substantial estimates: <verbatim|primaryT>,
    <verbatim|salaryT>, and <verbatim|gasT>'s local-card derivations and the
    five component estimates feeding <verbatim|decorate>. These are not
    implied by the budget/threshold lemmas.
  </itemize-minus>

